import ImperativeOptimization.ThumbData

/-!
# Loop counters in the high registers

GCC compiles Cortex-M0 loops with their counters and limits in `r8`-`r12` (Thumb-1 has few
low registers; `MOV`, `ADD` and `CMP` reach the high ones). `effect` models these three
exactly on `r0`-`r12` (the variables `rv`: `20`-`24` for `r8`-`r12`), and a call keeps
`r4`-`r11` under the assumption `abi` (the AAPCS), not `r12`. Two functions, with
certificates made by `benchmarks/cycles/binloops.py`:

```
f:  movs r0, #0; mov r8, r0; movs r1, #10; mov r9, r1
L:  movs r2, #1; add r8, r2; cmp r8, r9; bne L; bx lr
```

9 back edges, 65 cycles (`exHi_*`); the same loop with `bl g` at its head (`exHc_*`: `push
{lr}` ... `pop {pc}`, `g` a `bx lr`), 9 back edges, 139 cycles, which needs `r8` and `r9`
kept by the call. Refused: a smaller bound, the comparison with `r10` (nothing known), the
counter in `r12` across the call.
-/

